# PROBE negative-assertion. r(a, b) and its negative assertion make the ontology inconsistent.
# construct: NegativeObjectPropertyAssertion
# expect: inconsistent

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual . :b a owl:NamedIndividual .
:a :r :b .
[] a owl:NegativePropertyAssertion ; owl:sourceIndividual :a ; owl:assertionProperty :r ; owl:targetIndividual :b .
